module bindings.go.cloneSymlinkFilterBypass;

// go-git documents PlainClone and PlainCloneContext as cloning "a repository
// from the given URL" into the given path, and Clone and CloneContext as
// cloning into the worktree filesystem the caller supplies -- the checkout
// `git clone` performs, so every tree entry the repository declares is written
// to that filesystem, and a mode-120000 entry is written as a symbolic link
// pointing where the repository says. A clone of a repository whose content is
// not the cloner's own is therefore an extraction that reproduces link entries
// verbatim into the destination (CWE-22/CWE-59): the application's own later
// open through the checked-out path resolves wherever the link points.
//
// The documented ways to keep that materialisation off the host all appear
// here, and any one of them means link entries are decided by the cloning
// code rather than by the repository. A worktree filesystem that is not the
// host's -- go-billy's memfs is in memory, so nothing materialises on disk --
// is one. A wrapper or inspection that names symlinks is the other: the
// wrapping filesystem whose Symlink refuses, an os.ModeSymlink or
// filemode.ModeSymlink mode test, or the link-mode sentinel error, all leave
// an identifier or selector mentioning one in the function. A resolution
// probe on the result (filepath.EvalSymlinks, os.Readlink, os.Lstat) reads
// the same way. None of those forms reports.
//
// The call must be qualified to report. go-git's own forwarders call
// PlainCloneContext and CloneContext unqualified from inside the package, and
// a binding reading those bodies would report the library to itself, so the
// clause reads the qualified spelling every caller outside the package uses.
binding goGitCloneWithoutSymlinkDefense {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "go" and containsAny(node.context.callPath, [".PlainClone", ".CloneContext"]) and not (node.context.identifier contains "Symlink") and not (node.context.selector contains "Symlink") and not (node.context.callPath contains "memfs") and not containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["filepath.EvalSymlinks", "os.Readlink", "os.Lstat"])
  emit issue code.ArchiveSymlinkFilterBypass at node
}
